{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular octahedron is formed by joining the centers of adjoining faces of a cube. The ratio of the volume of the octahedron to the volume of the cube is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf42e665496b60f73f09a5f139effb16f4a7e088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{16} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\frac{1}{6} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\frac{1}{4} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"378\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the length of a side of the cube x. Thus, the volume of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. We can then find that a side of this regular octahedron is the square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca52b0958f3f9f59d7e2b415009ea2bd6e46c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{x}{2})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"33\" />+<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca52b0958f3f9f59d7e2b415009ea2bd6e46c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{x}{2})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"33\" /> which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88cc6d4aac3d9a7cfe2dd796471b38d85668e516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"41\" />. Using our general formula for the volume of a regular octahedron of side length a, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06df369eb066515c316a9006b1fa605c891ad0dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^3\\sqrt2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"41\" />, we get that the volume of this octahedron is...\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f365ab41183531c5cc11d8f9452af816503a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{x\\sqrt{2}}{2})^3 \\rightarrow \\frac{x^3\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\rightarrow \\frac{x^3\\sqrt{2}}{4}*\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\rightarrow \\frac{2x^3}{12}=\\frac{x^3}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"357\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Comparing the ratio of the volume of the octahedron to the cube is…\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc5f5b7a768136f6095cf605e7fe9bf04ca0f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{x^3}{6}}{x^3} \\rightarrow \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"44\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7ef72cd47d554d4b473d7e68935e75a19c0e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Split the cube in half along a cross-section parallel to two of the bases. Because of symmetry, we only need to compare the remaining square pyramid and the octahedron. Because the area of the base of the pyramid is half the area of the square base of the pyramid, and we divide by three for the pyramid's volume, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580e53a71e3e4e5c38ef6cc61553b0a11ad0a895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7ef72cd47d554d4b473d7e68935e75a19c0e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl